{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations","id":1511205,"title":"Did we ever get canon Tribal populations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T03:29:39-07:00","id":1511205,"title":"Did we ever get canon Tribal populations?","content":"I know that some 2nd ed and Revised books were interested in sticking populations onto things, despite these raising difficult questions (if there are only X members of Y, how are there Z numbers of subgroups).<br /> <br /> I'm aware that the BSDs are the largest Tribe, followed by the Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia who are all said to be &quot;the three largest Tribes&quot; (of the Garou Nation, that is!). But how would it pan out for the rest?<br /> <br /> I would imagine that the Red Talons and Stargazers are relatively rare, for differing reasons, and that Younger Brother would be quite rare.<br /> <br /> If there are any canon numbers I would probably just hold onto the proportions and drop the exact numbers; &quot;there are 3x as many members of Tribe X as there are of Tribe Y&quot; is a handy statistic to have handy IC, and it helps give a sense that these are real groups and not just Things You Can Pick In Char-Gen; knowing your tribe is rare produces a sense of preciousness and pressure, a feeling that if you die pointlessly it will further doom a dying breed.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting that there's something that stands out about the four largest tribes:<br /> - the BSDs feel it is imperative to produce as many Metis as they can, the Dark Litany forbids nothing when it comes to Garou-Garou romance and breeding, and this pays dividends<br /> - the Glass Walkers are modernists who eschew many traditions and focus on the cutting edge, and are said to have more Metis than average, perhaps in part because they're a bit too human; they also have Kinfolk who take on more militaristic roles, and they've given up on Pure Breed entirely by choice<br /> - the Bone Gnawers focus on survival above other concerns, prioritize what works over what's &quot;the way things are done&quot;, and adopt the castoffs, bastards and Metis of all the other Tribes<br /> - the Children of Gaia emphasize equality, harmony, seek non-violent solutions when they are the right way forward, adopt the Metis of other Tribes, and explicitly ignore the tenet of &quot;not allowing your kin to suffer your illness&quot;, instead allowing themselves and their kin to reach a great age and continue to care for others and be cared for in turn<br /> <br /> What can we learn from this? Well it depends on your OOC/IC opinion, but I think it's pretty interesting. An argument could be made that tradition is an inhibiting factor for the Garou, or that inclusion and diversity have canonically proven to be strengthening factors. It's also worth noting that 2/4 of these Tribes lack Pure Breed entirely, 1/4 has a tenet of absolute equality, and 1/4 barely has Pure Breed at all (the vast majority of BSDs are Pure Breed 0, and only a select few with a direct line back to the Howlers have PB5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T04:48:01-07:00","id":1511211,"title":"","content":"Glass walkers are considered a small tribe IIRC? Too human, lots of wolf issues, reputation is poor, city caerns aren't that common etc. They adopt metis more than birth them<br /> <br /> Three largest tribes other than the corrupted should be BG (having no standards) CoG (having few standards) and Fianna (breeding like rabbits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T05:19:27-07:00","id":1511214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511211#post1511211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glass walkers are considered a small tribe IIRC? Too human, lots of wolf issues, reputation is poor, city caerns aren't that common etc. They adopt metis more than birth them<br /> <br /> Three largest tribes other than the corrupted should be BG (having no standards) CoG (having few standards) and Fianna (breeding like rabbits)</div> </div> </div> </div>See I thought they adopted most of their Metis, but W20 mentions them producing their own rather than adopting. The two Tribes who are mentioned to adopt Metis explicitly in their main writeup are the CoG and BGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T05:33:28-07:00","id":1511215,"title":"","content":"All tribes make metis<br /> The Glass walkers are commonly believed to make more per-capita because they're degenerates, but the GW in their tribe books state they have above-average levels because of adoption. <br /> <br /> That said tribe books tend to be a little more generous about things. For some reason, I recall one fianna book going as far as to be moderate when describing their usually vitriolic hatred for metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T06:37:07-07:00","id":1511217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511215#post1511215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All tribes make metis<br /> The Glass walkers are commonly believed to make more per-capita because they're degenerates, but the GW in their tribe books state they have above-average levels because of adoption.<br /> <br /> That said tribe books tend to be a little more generous about things. For some reason, I recall one fianna book going as far as to be moderate when describing their usually vitriolic hatred for metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a weird reading of &quot;As time went by, WW figured out some things were too much and tried to fix them through Revised&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T07:33:12-07:00","id":1511219,"title":"","content":"True<br /> WW:TA 1st edition - Lupus account for as little as 3% of the total Garou population<br /> WW:TA 2nd edition - Lupus account for as little as 13% of the total Garou population<br /> So a 10% difference between editions!<br /> \u200b<br /> A World of Rage,Rage Across Russia, Rage Across Australia, Rage Across Appalachia and Rage Across New York gives us a nice number breakdown:<br /> <br /> <b>Australia</b><br /> Total Garou population: 350.<br /> 25 Black Furies<br /> 40 Bone Gnawers<br /> 20 Children of Gaia<br /> 20 Get of Fenris<br /> 40 Glass Walkers<br /> 35 Fianna<br /> 35 Red Talons<br /> 20 Shadow Lords<br /> 15 Silent Striders<br /> 35 Silver Fangs<br /> 6 Stargazers<br /> 20 Uktena<br /> 1 Wendigo<br /> 40 Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> <b>Russia</b><br /> 75 Black Furies, with 35 centered around Blood of the Sea Sept<br /> At least 200 Bone Gnawers, 100 of which are affiliated with the Sept of the People's Will<br /> 45 Children of Gaia, with 20 at the White Sea Sept<br /> Very few Fianna, no number given.<br /> 105 Get of Fenris, with 35 organized around the Artic Axe Sept, 40 organized around the Sept of Fafnir's Brood, and 30 others.<br /> 88, formerly 105 Glass Walkers, with 40 organized around the Sept of the Learning Hall. 17 of the 40 members of the Sept of the Learning Hall were killed when it was destroyed by Baba Yaga's forces.<br /> Roughly 65 Red Talons, with 40 organized around the Winter Forest Sept, and roughly 25 others.<br /> Roughly 75 Shadow Lords, with 30 organized around the Brooding Sky Sept (which is actually in Ukraine, not Russia), 25 organized around the Thunderstrike Sept, and roughly 20 others.<br /> 20 Silent Striders, formerly 30, having had ten killed by Baba Yaga's forces.<br /> Roughly 100 Silver Fangs, with nearly 30 at the Sept of the Crescent Moon, and 70 more elsewhere. (note that these numbers are pre October 1996, which is when Baba Yaga destroyed the Aral Sea Caern of the Silver Fangs.)<br /> 22 Stargazers, with 15 at the Sept of the Crystal Mind, and seven more elsewhere.<br /> 51 Uktena, formerly 60, with about 26, formerly about 35 at the Spirit Stone Caern, after losing around 9 members when it was attacked by Baba Yaga in 1996, and 25 elsewhere.<br /> 30 Wendigo organized around the Sept of the Siberian Wilds. More may also be in other parts of the country.<br /> Unspecified number of Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> <b>New York State</b><br /> Total Garou population: ~373 (335 permanent inhabitants)<br /> 17 Black Furies<br /> 60 Bone Gnawers (49 in NYC)<br /> 33 Children of Gaia<br /> 30 Fianna<br /> 34 Get of Fenris<br /> 52 Glass Walkers (40 in NYC)<br /> 11 Red Talons<br /> 23 Shadow Lords<br /> 5 Silent Striders<br /> 18 Silver Fangs<br /> 2 Stargazers (regular visitors)<br /> 36 Uktena<br /> 36 Wendigos (from out of Ottawa)<br /> 16 Black Spiral Dancers<br /> <br /> <b>Southeastern Appalachia</b><br /> Total population: Between 150-200<br /> 12 Black Furies<br /> 20-30 Bone Gnawers<br /> 20 Children of Gaia<br /> 30 Fianna<br /> 20 Get of Fenris<br /> 15 Glass Walkers<br /> 1 Red Talon<br /> 1 Shadow Lord<br /> 4 Silent Striders<br /> 15 Silver Fangs<br /> 3 Stargazers<br /> 25 Uktena<br /> 1 Wendigo<br /> Unspecified number of Black Spiral Dancers<br /> These numbers are pre November 1, 1997, a day in which over 50 Garou were killed in battle<br /> <br /> These are of course age old editions; WW20 were more generous with the Garou numbers<br /> <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\">Eldagusto</a> </b>gathered some info on that many years ago.<br /> In modern times the Garou are estimated at over 10k but under 20k, though W20 seems to be rather more generous with population Numbers, revised gave a breakdown.<br /> Basically Stargazers are rarest and may number at about 200, but once again W20 seems to imply they are more common then that, with Red Talons at about 400. Bone Gnawers are most populous and may be at about 2k, and Spirals are said to be bigger then any two Gaian Tribes putting them at 3-4k+. And generally populous tribes range from 800-1400. There are a few peculiarities, they seem to number sub tribes like Hakken as equal in size to their main tribes, but I really think Hakken should be more 400 Garou in size rather then the assumed 1400 of the main Shadowlords, otherwise you have Grandfather Thunder with more followers then rat, and the Wang Tong should have been listed along with the Boli Zhouhisze as a sub tribe, thus inflating Rat's followers to more towards 3k then 2k.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> And some liek to use the quasi-cannon 1:35 000 ratio (means 8700 Garou in the US more or less)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T07:50:11-07:00","id":1511220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511217#post1511217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a weird reading of &quot;As time went by, WW figured out some things were too much and tried to fix them through Revised&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think they overcorrected. Plus there's a lot of -I am a fan of X tribe, my characters are X tribe and perhaps I identify with them a little too much, I'd like my character to be representative of X tribe/In my game I got my tribe to make progress, so I will portray X tribe as moderate or as positively as I can-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T08:26:00-07:00","id":1511224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511220#post1511220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think they overcorrected. Plus there's a lot of -I am a fan of X tribe, my characters are X tribe and perhaps I identify with them a little too much, I'd like my character to be representative of X tribe/In my game I got my tribe to make progress, so I will portray X tribe as moderate or as positively as I can-</div> </div> </div> </div>They did not. Children of Gaia nonwhitstanding, the Revised Tribebooks were the best iterations of the Garou Nation we've had. Some of the backlash we've gotten for W20's protrayal of Garou come from them rolling back the changes and the ideas that came along with Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T08:58:38-07:00","id":1511231,"title":"","content":"What I've read is that Stargazers now number less than 500 worldwide and that the BSD are the equivalent of 10% of the world's Garou population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T10:09:29-07:00","id":1511235,"title":"","content":"Tribe books sometimes do just feel like they were written by a fan of the tribe, for fans of the tribe. Not a bad thing by any means but it means you end up with a tribe book that goes &quot;oh we aren't REALLY bad in the one major way our Tribe is meant to be bad... when you really actually think about it, if you listen to us, who are impartial, we have no flaws at all-&quot;<br /> <br /> Like we're told Fianna hate Metis. But then the NPCs you're meant to like don't. And none of the PCs do, obviously! And so you're left wondering who these notably Metis-hating Fianna even are!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T10:10:02-07:00","id":1511236,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> thanks for the breakdown! Really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:01:04-07:00","id":1511256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511235#post1511235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribe books sometimes do just feel like they were written by a fan of the tribe, for fans of the tribe. Not a bad thing by any means but it means you end up with a tribe book that goes &quot;oh we aren't REALLY bad in the one major way our Tribe is meant to be bad... when you really actually think about it, if you listen to us, who are impartial, we have no flaws at all-&quot;<br /> <br /> Like we're told Fianna hate Metis. But then the NPCs you're meant to like don't. And none of the PCs do, obviously! And so you're left wondering who these notably Metis-hating Fianna even are!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, when it comes to WOD, I think that tribes, clans and traditions have a lot to do with their stereotypes, not entirely, but that they are not there for nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:18:19-07:00","id":1511281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511231#post1511231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I've read is that Stargazers now number less than 500 worldwide and that the BSD are the equivalent of 10% of the world's Garou population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the Stargazers should be taken at its face. The tribe's been plagued by Asian stereotypes and questionable numbers since the beginning of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:59:03-07:00","id":1511296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511219#post1511219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True<br /> WW:TA 1st edition - Lupus account for as little as 3% of the total Garou population<br /> WW:TA 2nd edition - Lupus account for as little as 13% of the total Garou population<br /> So a 10% difference between editions!<br /> \u200b<br /> A World of Rage,Rage Across Russia, Rage Across Australia, Rage Across Appalachia and Rage Across New York gives us a nice number breakdown:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd not take any values given back in 1st Edition as relevant to what Werewolf would become. With the spread around the world, the Wolves became a much bigger thing than the original designers intended. Where did you find these numbers in A World of Rage? Been using that a lot recently so it's fresh in memory. That thing seems to be intentionally nebulous about its numbers and it refers to numbers only in context to certain events. For instance it says that 44 Red Talons have dissapeared in Australia recently. It's considered a problem and a plot hook, but it's not treated as 1/6th of all Garou in Australia disappearing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:35:29-07:00","id":1511297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511235#post1511235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribe books sometimes do just feel like they were written by a fan of the tribe, for fans of the tribe. Not a bad thing by any means but it means you end up with a tribe book that goes &quot;oh we aren't REALLY bad in the one major way our Tribe is meant to be bad... when you really actually think about it, if you listen to us, who are impartial, we have no flaws at all-&quot;<br /> <br /> Like we're told Fianna hate Metis. But then the NPCs you're meant to like don't. And none of the PCs do, obviously! And so you're left wondering who these notably Metis-hating Fianna even are!</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading the book in question would actually help with this feeling you have. First of all, the early tribes are horrible caricatures defined by grimderp left and right - the less said about the Drunken idiots that the Fianna were and the Supremacist Vikings the Get were, the better (We can find many stupid ideas on the original tribebooks, but these two are good as most people know the bullshit by heart). Secondly, the Revised tribebooks actually go into the nuance of these things.<br /> <br /> Of course the Fianna are prone to loose relationships and metis popping up, they are even worse about considering what it means for them and how to take responsibility over those actions. They actually go into that in depth and how the life of a metis works out in a Fianna Sept and what can be expected out of it and how it can go good and bad. It even has differing views by multiple voices on how these things work out so you have even more depth about this. This would continue with all the other developments of the Fianna spreading accross the world with the celtic cultures rather than the whole &quot;Oh we must have the Irish in a US-centric RPG, and let's make them bad stereotypes&quot;. Of course, making them more sensible and less of a caricature didn't erase the fact that they can still be idiots and that their culture actually reinforces certain bad patterns that will bite them in the back and create tension for the players to engage with.<br /> <br /> The Get are obsessed with prowess and strength. But they are not actually coddling a bunch of white supremacists and Aesir cryptofascists in their midst, they have fought their own battle against their supremacists and wiped them out for they were a stain on their honor and the fact that power comes from different places. The idea that the Get are actually the children of Fenris and that the Aesir are the villians of their tale was brilliant, removing the problem collecting camp was a solid plan. Pointing out that they take anyone who fulfills their criteria of Strength and how Pure Breed is not a facet of Strength was the right choice. Yet still they are proud, they are teritorrial, they are assholes looking for a fight and to prove to everyone how awesome they are. They are still a deeply troubled tribe, but not one staffed with morons but with people.<br /> <br /> The idea is to make these concepts playable. There are still warts and problems to resolve and generate conflict, however it's not defined by there being flaws based around racial purity or being a drunk. Instead of getting caricatures we actually get organisations with history and context that stand on their own with the postulations we've had about how they should be working since the start. What was done there was the best effort to make Werewolf into a better game.<br /> <br /> For bonus points, also back in 2000, Revised said that Metis and M\u00e9tis are different things with different pronunciation, and that it was not the intent to invoke the people in question with that name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T05:43:21-07:00","id":1511347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511296#post1511296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you find these numbers in A World of Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>World of Rage describes the effects of Baba Yaga's attacks on around p. 74<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T06:53:16-07:00","id":1511348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511205-did-we-ever-get-canon-tribal-populations?p=1511347#post1511347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> World of Rage describes the effects of Baba Yaga's attacks on around p. 74</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it says X have died. It doesn't say &quot;Russia has X Garou of these, these and these tribes&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:58:46-07:00","id":1511388,"title":"","content":"Thats why I wrote A World of Rage,Rage Across Russia, Rage Across Australia, Rage Across Appalachia and Rage Across New York gives us a nice number breakdown; ment to use together<br /> <br /> For example, in Rage across Russia, from p 54, to p 77 (or 78 if you want the Siberkah) you will find the Tribe-breakdown and in every tribe's Sept description you will find the numbers too<br /> And so on in the other materials too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}